// `__array_new__` with an f32 FILL bound WITHOUT an annotation. `vl check` returns 0 and the
// module did not validate — clause 1. The checker calls the call `f32[]` at both spellings;
// `exprF32Array` lacked the `__array_new__` arm its i64/f64/string/ref siblings carry, so the
// binding claimed no list kind and took a bare `i32` cell while `array.new $fa32` pushed the
// wrapper into it. The annotated destination is the control.
// Should print 7.75.
function mk(): f32 { 7.5 }
const xs = __array_new__(2, mk())
print(xs[1] + 0.25)
